==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|menos}}, displacing collateral form {{m|roa-opt|mẽos}}, from {{der|pt|la|minus}}, neuter of {{m|pt|minor|t=lesser; smaller}}, comparative of {{m|pt|parvus|t=small}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA}}
* {{hyph|pt|me|nos}}

===Adverb===
{{pt-adv|hascomp=no}}

# [[less]] {{gloss|in lower degree}}
#: {{ant|pt|mais}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Aqui é '''menos''' frio.|Here is '''less''' cold.}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Se trabalhares '''menos''', cansarás '''menos'''.|If you work '''less''', you will tire '''less'''.}}

===Preposition===
{{head|pt|preposition}}

# [[except]]; [[but]]
#: {{syn|pt|exceto|fora}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Li todos, '''menos''' o último.|I read all, '''except''' the last one.}}
# {{lb|pt|mathematics}} [[minus]] {{gloss|indicates subtraction}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Três '''menos''' dois é um.|Three '''minus''' two is one.}}

===Pronoun===
{{pt-pron|mf|pl=menos}}

# [[fewer]] {{gloss|a smaller number of}}, [[less]] {{gloss|a smaller size or significance of}}
#: {{ant|pt|mais}}
#: {{uxi|pt|'''Menos''' pessoas correm.|'''Fewer''' people run.}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Atirou com '''menos''' precisão.|He shot with '''less''' precision.}}

====Usage notes====
* Some use the feminine plural {{m|pt|menas}}. It is only used in Brazil. Such usage is non-standard and highly proscribed.

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|m}}

# [[minus sign]] {{gloss|the symbol −}}
#: {{syn|pt|sinal de menos}}

